1. What is an object type in TypeScript?

An object type defines the expected structure of an object, including its property names and types.

const user: {
    name: string;
    age: number;
} = {
    name: "Bhargav",
    age: 27
};

2. What is a type alias?

A type alias allows us to give a reusable name to a type using the type keyword.

type User = {
    name: string;
    age: number;
};

const user: User = {
    name: "Bhargav",
    age: 27
};

3. What is an interface in TypeScript?

An interface defines a contract describing the structure an object must satisfy.

interface User {
    name: string;
    age: number;
}

Any object declared as User must contain the required properties with the correct types.
